    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0225" n="191" xml:id="pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 136.</note>
                <head>Mr. Davis to Mr. Bancroft.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. <hi rendition="#small-caps">219.]</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 17, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Inclosed you will find a copy of Mr.
                    Washburne’s dispatch, No. 238, on the subject of the departure of North Germans
                    from French territory.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Mr. Washburne’s course in this correspondence has been approved. He advises the
                    Department, in a dispatch received to-day, that he has received a reply to his
                    note, which will be forwarded, he says, by the next post. As soon as it is
                    received here, a copy will be sent you.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. B. DAVIS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For this inclosure see Mr. Washburne’s No. 238, dated July 29, under the
                        title “France,” <hi rendition="#italic">ante.</hi>]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
